 folga em 31 de dezembro, o descanso vai de 29 de dezembro a 1 de janeiro</li></ul><p>Caem na quarta-feira: Dia do Trabalho (1 de maio); Dia Nacional de Zumbi e da Consciência Negra (20 de novembro); Natal (25 de dezembro). Para virar viagem é preciso emendar dois dias, o que costuma exigir negociar a folga.</p><p>Coincidem com o fim de semana e não geram folga extra: Tiradentes (domingo, 21 de abril); Independência do Brasil (sábado, 7 de setembro); Nossa Senhora Aparecida (sábado, 12 de outubro); Finados (sábado, 2 de novembro).</p><h2>2030 comparado com 2029</h2><p>2030 tem 6 feriados em dia de semana, contra 9 em 2029: 2030 tem 3 dias úteis a mais que 2029. Mudam de dia da semana em relação a 2029: Confraternização Universal (Ano Novo) passa de segunda-feira para terça-feira; Tiradentes passa de sábado para domingo; Dia do Trabalho passa de terça-feira para quarta-feira; Independência do Brasil passa de sexta-feira para sábado; Nossa Senhora Aparecida passa de sexta-feira para sábado; Finados passa de sexta-feira para sábado; Proclamação da República passa de quinta-feira para sexta-feira; Dia Nacional de Zumbi e da Consciência Negra passa de terça-feira para quarta-feira.</p>", "faq": [{"q": "Quantos dias úteis tem 2030 no Brasil?", "a": "Considerando só os feriados nacionais, 2030 tem 255 dias úteis de segunda a sexta (de 261 dias de semana no calendário)."}, {"q": "Qual é o maior período sem feriado em 2030?", "a": "De quarta-feira, 1 de maio até sábado, 7 de setembro, são 129 dias sem nenhum feriado nacional."}, {"q": "Quantos fins de semana prolongados tem 2030?", "a": "2 fins de semana de três dias formados por feriados em segunda ou sexta-feira, mais 1 oportunidades de emenda em terça ou quinta."}]}}, "us-holidays-2025": {"en": {"article": "<h2>2025 by the numbers: working days and gaps between holidays</h2><p>The first federal holiday of 2025 is New Year's Day (Wednesday, January 1) and the last is Christmas Day (Thursday, December 25). Of the 261 Monday-to-Friday days in the year, <strong>250</strong> remain working days once weekday holidays are removed.</p><p>The longest stretch with no holiday runs from Monday, February 17 to Monday, May 26: 98 calendar days without an official day off. The shortest gap separates Washington's Birthday (Presidents Day) and Memorial Day, only 15 days apart. The busiest month is January with 2. Months with no holiday: March, April, August.</p><h2>Long weekends in 2025</h2><p>Holidays on a Monday or Friday create a three-day weekend without using any vacation time. In 2025 there are 6:</p><ul><li><strong>Martin Luther King Jr. Day</strong> — Monday, January 18–20</li><li><strong>Washington's Birthday (Presidents Day)</strong> — Monday, February 15–17</li><li><strong>Memorial Day</strong> — Monday, May 24–26</li><li><strong>Independence Day</strong> — Friday, July 4–6</li><li><strong>Labor Day</strong> — Monday, August 30 – September 1</li><li><strong>Columbus Day</strong> — Monday, October 11–13</li></ul><p>Holidays on a Tuesday or Thursday can be stretched into four days off with a single vacation day:</p><ul><li><strong>Juneteenth National Independence Day</strong> (Thursday, June 19) — take June 20 off and rest from June 19–22</li><li><strong>Veterans Day</strong> (Tuesday, November 11) — take November 10 off and rest from November 8–11</li><li><strong>Thanksgiving Day</strong> (Thursday, November 27) — take November 28 off and rest from November 27–30</li><li><strong>Christmas Day</strong> (Thursday, December 25) — take December 26 off and rest from December 25–28</li></ul><p>Falling on a Wednesday: New Year's Day (January 1). Making a trip out of these needs two vacation days.</p><h2>2025 compared with 2026</h2><p>2025 has 11 weekday holidays against 11 in 2026. Weekday changes versus 2026: New Year's Day moves from Thursday to Wednesday; Juneteenth National Independence Day moves from Friday to Thursday; Veterans Day moves from Wednesday to Tuesday; Christmas Day moves from Friday to Thursday.</p>", "faq": [{"q": "How many working days are there in 2025?", "a": "Counting only the holidays listed above, 2025 has 250 working days out of 261 Monday-to-Friday days."}, {"q": "What is the longest stretch without a holiday in 2025?", "a": "From Monday, February 17 to Monday, May 26: 98 days with no official holiday."}, {"q": "How many long weekends does 2025 have?", "a": "6 three-day weekends from Monday or Friday holidays, plus 4 bridge opportunities on Tuesdays or Thursdays."}]}}, "us-holidays-2026": {"en": {"article": "<h2>2026 by the numbers: working days and gaps between holidays</h2><p>The first federal holiday of 2026 is New Year's Day (Thursday, January 1) and the last is Christmas Day (Friday, December 25). After subtracting holidays that fall on weekdays, 250 working days are left out of 261 weekdays in 2026.</p><p>The longest stretch with no holiday runs from Monday, February 16 to Monday, May 25: 98 calendar days without an official day off. The shortest gap separates Washington's Birthday (Presidents Day) and Memorial Day, only 14 days apart. The busiest month is January with 2. Months with no holiday: March, April, August.</p><h2>Long weekends in 2026</h2><p>Holidays on a Monday or Friday create a three-day weekend without using any vacation time. In 2026 there are 8:</p><ul><li><strong>Martin Luther King Jr. Day</strong> — Monday, January 17–19</li><li><strong>Washington's Birthday (Presidents Day)</strong> — Monday, February 14–16</li><li><strong>Memorial Day</strong> — Monday, May 23–25</li><li><strong>Juneteenth National Independence Day</strong> — Friday, June 19–21</li><li><strong>Independence Day</strong> — Friday, July 3–5</li><li><strong>Labor Day</strong> — Monday, September 5–7</li><li><strong>Columbus Day</strong> — Monday, October 10–12</li><li><strong>Christmas Day</strong> — Friday, December 25–27</li></ul><p>Holidays on a Tuesday or Thursday can be stretched into four days off with a single vacation day:</p><ul><l